= The Count's Doubts

Through the comm code he left with Bail Organa years ago, **Count Dooku** sends a private message. He speaks of a master who has promised him a new order, one free of corruption, and who has begun to treat him like a servant to be discarded. He hints that his master is someone in the Senate, close to its very heart.

In exchange for amnesty and real reform of the Senate, he will give the Caucus a name.

- @accept: Accept. Amnesty for the truth.
- @refuse: Refuse. We do not bargain with butchers.

@accept
subtitle: [? if rim_enfranchised or anti_corruption : Our reforms make our promises credible. ?][? if not rim_enfranchised and not anti_corruption : He may not believe we can deliver reform. ?]
on-arrival: {!
var c = 0.3 + (Q.rim_enfranchised ? 0.15 : 0) + (Q.anti_corruption ? 0.15 : 0) + (Q.federal_compact ? 0.15 : 0) + Q.dooku_doubt * 0.03 - Q.grand_plan / 400;
if (Math.random() < c) { Q.dooku_turned = 1; Q.evidence += 4; Q.jedi_suspicion += 3; Q.war_balance += 1; this.achieve('dooku_turned'); }
else { Q.dooku_failed = 1; Q.peace_talks -= 1; Q.investigators_lost += 1; }
!}

[? if dooku_turned : The name arrives on an encrypted datacard: **Darth Sidious is [? if pal_chancellor : Supreme Chancellor ?][? if not pal_chancellor : Senator ?]Palpatine.** With it come years of evidence: holograms, payments, orders. Dooku himself vanishes into hiding. ?][? if dooku_failed : The meeting is a trap, or perhaps someone was listening. Our envoy never returns. Dooku's next broadcast is more violent than ever. ?]

@refuse
on-arrival: hawk_dissent -= 3; dooku_doubt -= 2

The Caucus does not reply. Dooku's doubts, if they were real, die with the message.
